1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Virginia de Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #3127, b. 29 May 1568, d. 25 March 1615
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=18 Jan 2003
2 CONT
2 CONT      Virginia de Medici was born on 29 May 1568. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Cosimo I de Medici, Granduca di Toscana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Cesar d'Este, Duca di Modena, son of unknown d'Este, on 6 February 1586. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 25 March 1615 at age 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Virginia de Medici and Cesar d'Este, Duca di Modena
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Alfonso III d'Este, Duca di Modena+ b. 20 Oct 1591, d. 24 May 1644
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p313.htm#i3127
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_de%27_Medici
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Virginia de' Medici (May 29, 1568 – January 15, 1615) was a daughter of Cosimo I de' Medici, Grand Duke of Tuscany and Camilla Martelli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia was born on 29 May 1568, two years before her parents married. She was the only child of Cosimo I de' Medici, grand duke of Tuscany, and his second wife Camilla Martelli. In 1581 she had been promised in marriage to Franc
2 CONC esco Sforza di Santa Fiora, but he changed his mind and renounced the world to accept the Cardinal's hat and privileges from the hands of Pope Gregory XIII. On 6 February 1586 Virginia married Caesare d'Este, duke of Modena, son o
2 CONC f Alfonso d'Este, lord of Montecchio, and Giulia della Rovere. They had ten children of whom three sons and a daughter would have progeny. Virginia died on 15 January 1615; some said she was poisoned by her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 6, 1586, she married Cesare d'Este, Duke of Modena and Reggio from 1597.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 10 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Giulia d'Este (1588–1645)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso III d'Este (1591–1644), Duke of Modena from 1628
2 CONT
2 CONT Luigi d'Este (1593/1594–1664), Lord of Montecchio and Scandiano
2 CONT
2 CONT Laura d'Este (1594–1630)
2 CONT
2 CONT Caterina d'Este (1595–1618)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ippolito d'Este (1599–1647)
2 CONT
2 CONT Niccolo d'Este (1601–1640)
2 CONT
2 CONT Borso d'Este (1605–1657), maternal grandfather of Victor Amadeus of Savoy, Prince of Carignan
2 CONT
2 CONT Foresto d'Este (1606–1639/1640)
2 CONT
2 CONT Angela Caterina d'Este (died 1651), a nun of the Catholic Church
2 CONT
2 CONT In her later years, she suffered from insanity. She died in 1615, and was buried in Modena, at the Church of San Vincenzo
