1 OCCU Duc d'Anjou (1640-1660), duc d'Orléans, de Chartres and de Valois (May 1661-1701), duc de Nemours (24 April 1672-1701), duc de Montpensier (20 April 1695-1701), dauphin d'Auvergne (1693), prince de Joinville and de La Roche-sur-Yo
2 CONC n, Dud d'Orléans
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch
2 CONT *Philippe I, Duke of Orléans
2 CONT *Royal house
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/projects/House-of-Orl%C3%A9ans House d'Orléans]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT First marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Married his first cousin, Princess Henrietta of England, daughter of Charles I of England and Henrietta Maria of France, on 31 March 1661, at the Palais Royal. The couple had three children, in addition to four miscarriages and on
2 CONC e stillborn:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Marie Louise d'Orléans (26 March 1662 – 12 February 1689) married Charles II of Spain, no issue.
2 CONT # Miscarriage (1663).[109]
2 CONT # Philippe Charles d'Orléans, Duke of Valois (16 July 1664 – 8 December 1666) died in infancy.
2 CONT # Stillborn daughter (9 July 1665).
2 CONT # Miscarriage (1666).[109]
2 CONT # Miscarriage (1667).[109]
2 CONT # Miscarriage (1668).[110]
2 CONT # Anne Marie d'Orléans (27 August 1669 – 26 August 1728) married Victor Amadeus II, Duke of Savoy (future king of Sardinia) and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Elizabeth Charlotte of the Palatinate, daughter of Charles I Louis, Elector Palatine and Charlotte of Hesse-Kassel,[70] on 16 November 1671 at Châlons. The couple had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Alexandre Louis d'Orléans, Duke of Valois (2 June 1673 – 16 March 1676) died in childhood;
2 CONT # Philippe II, Duke of Orléans (2 August 1674 – 2 December 1723) married Françoise Marie de Bourbon, Légitimée de France, and had issue;
2 CONT # Élisabeth Charlotte d'Orléans (13 September 1676 – 24 December 1744) married Leopold, Duke of Lorraine, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p10140.htm#i101396 '''The Peerage'''] 
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/F/per_page.php?id=4094 '''Geneall''']
2 CONT *[http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_d%27Orl%C3%A9ans_%281640-1701%29 '''Wikipedia - Français''']
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_I,_Duke_of_Orl%C3%A9ans '''Wikipedia - English''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In the autumn of 1647, at age seven, Philippe caught smallpox, but recovered and convalesced at the Palais-Royal.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippe_I,_Duke_of_Orl%C3%A9ans
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Filip I (21. syyskuuta 1640, Saint-Germain-en-Laye – 9. kesäkuuta 1701, Saint-Cloud), jota kutsuttiin myös Ranskan Filipiksi tai Monsieur'ksi, oli Ranskan kuninkaan Ludvig XIV:n nuorempi veli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hänen tittelinsä olivat moninaiset, esimerkiksi Ranskan perintöruhtinas, Orléansin herttua, Anjoun herttua (vuoteen 1668 asti), Chartresin herttua, Valois'n herttua ja Joinvillen ruhtinas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Filipistä polveutui Ranskan hallitsijasuvun, Bourbonien nuorempi haara eli Orléans-suku, joka hallitsi Ranskaa vuosina 1830–1848.
