2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de France[1], Son of France, Duke of Burgundy (duc de Bourgogne), and later Dauphin of France (16 August 1682 – 18 February 1712) was the eldest son of Louis, Dauphin of France, known as le Grand Dauphin. He was himself some
2 CONC times known as le Petit Dauphin, having become Dauphin of France upon his father's death in 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
