1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A9opold_Cl%C3%A9ment,_Hereditary_Prince_of_Lorraine en.wikipedia.org...] ; 
2 CONT ===Full name===
2 CONT Léopold Clément Charles de Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Léopold Clément, Hereditary Prince of Lorraine (Léopold Clément Charles; 25 April 1707 – 4 June 1723)[1] was heir apparent to the throne of the sovereign Duchy of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was the reigning Duke of Lorraine and his mother a member of the House of Bourbon, then ruling the Kingdom of France. He became the Hereditary Prince at the death of his older brother Louis in 1711, but died of smallpox
2 CONC  in 1723 at the age of sixteen, unmarried and without descendants.
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born at the [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fichier:Chateau_Luneville_ar_10_2010.JPG '''Château de Lunéville'''] to Léopold, Duke of Lorraine and his wife Élisabeth Charlotte d'Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Léopold was the third son born to his parents. His eldest brother, also Léopold (1669–1700), died aged eight months. Three other older siblings died in an outbreak of smallpox at Lunéville: Élisabeth Charlotte (1700–1711), Marie G
2 CONC abrièle Charlotte (1702–1711) and Louis (1704–1711). The smallpox epidemic had killed other royalty such as the Grand Dauphin and the Holy Roman Emperor Joseph I at the same time.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1722 Léopold also became the heir to the Duchy of Teschen which was given to his father in compensation for his father's maternal grandmother's rights to the Duchy of Montferrat in northern Italy, which Emperor Charles VI had t
2 CONC aken and given to his allies, the Dukes of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1723 he was sent to Vienna to carry out his education under the supervision of Charles VI, his father's first cousin. Another reason for his journey was to forge a Habsburg-Lorraine alliance through a marriage with the Archduch
2 CONC ess Maria Theresa.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon afterward the prince caught smallpox at Lunéville and quickly died at the Château there. He was buried in the Ducal Crypt at the Church of Saint-François-des-Cordeliers, Nancy. His younger brother Francis Stephen became the H
2 CONC ereditary Prince and later married Maria Theresa, Habsburg heiress and future Queen regnant of Hungry and Bohemia.
2 CONT
