2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p10307.htm#i103069 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://geneall.net/de/name/384918/joseph-ferdinand-leopold-herzog-von-bayern/ Geneall]
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Ferdinand_of_Bavaria_(1692-1699)_ Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Joseph Ferdinand Leopold of Bavaria, also known as Infante Jose Fernando de Baviera y Austria, Prince of Asturias (28 October 1692 - 6 February 1699) was the son of Maximilian II Emanuel, Elector of Bavaria (1679-1705, 1714-1
2 CONC 726) and his first wife, Maria Antonia of Austria, daughter of Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor, maternal granddaughter of King Felipe IV of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT A family tree showing the relationships of the various claimants to Charles II
2 CONT
2 CONT Before the War of the Spanish Succession, Joseph Ferdinand was the favored choice of the Kingdom of England and the Dutch Republic to succeed as the ruler of Spain, young Charles II of Spain chose him as his heir. The unexpected d
2 CONC eath of Joseph Ferdinand in 1699 at the age of six rendered the Anglo-French treaty inoperative and led to the Second Partition Treaty (1700), agreed upon by France, England, and the Netherlands; under its terms, Philip of Anjou w
2 CONC as to receive the Kingdom of Naples, Kingdom of Sicily and the Duchy of Milan, while the rest of the Spanish dominions were to go to Charles, son of Leopold I. But Leopold did not accept this treaty and Louis XIV of France broke t
2 CONC he treaty, when he enthroned Philip in Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, also known as Infante Joseph Ferdinand of Spain, was a result of extreme inbreeding within Spanish Habsburg dynasty. Joseph Ferdinand's mother's (Maria Antonia of Austria) immediate pedigree was exceptionally loaded with n
2 CONC ieces giving birth to children of their uncles: Maria Antonia was daughter of Margarita of Spain and Emperor Leopold I, Margarita being Leopold's niece, being daughter of Marie-Anne of Austria and Philip IV of Spain, that Marie-An
2 CONC ne (Maria Antonia's aunt and grandmother) being Philip's niece - was also daughter of Maria Ana of Spain (1606-46) and Emperor Ferdinand III, who were Leopold's parents too. Thus, Empress Maria Ana was simultaneously argarita's au
2 CONC nt, mother-in-law and grandmother. Joseph Ferdinand's great-uncle was the so-called Bewitched Charles II of Spain, who was the degenerated last Habsburg monarch of Spain, whom Joseph was destined to succeed, had he not himself pre
2 CONC deceased Charles.
