1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Lord Dacre1
2 CONT *'''M, #30026, b. 20 April 1717, d. 12 January 1786
2 CONT *Last Edited=21 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.78%
2 CONT *''' Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Lord Dacre, was born on 20 April 1717.1 He was the son of Richard Barrett and Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre.1 He married Anna Maria Pratt, daughter of Sir John Pratt and Elizabeth Wilson, on 15 May
2 CONC  1739 at London, England.1 He died on 12 January 1786 at age 68 at London, England, without surviving issue.1
2 CONT *'''     He was given the name of Thomas Barrett at birth.1 He was educated at Harrow School, Harrow on the Hill, London, England.1 He succeeded to the title of 17th Lord Dacre [E., 1321] on 26 June 1755.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Lord Dacre and Anna Maria Pratt
2 CONT **1.Hon. Anne Barbara Barrett-Lennard1 b. 1740, d. 14 Mar 1749
2 CONT *'''Child of Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Lord Dacre and unknown Fitzthomas
2 CONT **1.Sir Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 1st Bt., +3 b. 6 Jan 1762, d. 25 Jun 1857
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1014. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.[S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 271.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p3003.htm#i30026 __________
2 CONT *Anne Lennard, Countess of Sussex (25 February 1661-2 – 16 May 1721-2), formerly Lady Anne Palmer, alias Fitzroy, was the eldest daughter of Barbara Palmer née Villiers, 1st Duchess of Cleveland, and most likely Charles II of Engl
2 CONC and or Philip Stanhope, 2nd Earl of Chesterfield.  ....
2 CONT *Anne's husband, the Earl of Sussex, was a "popular but extravagant man"[5] who, by extravagance and losses from gambling, had to sell the estate of Herstmonceaux and others. Lord and Lady Sussex separated in 1688. She was widowed
2 CONC  in 1715.  ....
2 CONT *The children of her union with Sussex were two sons, who died in infancy; and two daughters, who lived to adulthood, co-heirs of the Barony Dacre:[6]  ....
2 CONT **4.Anne Lennard: born 17 August 1684 at Sussex; died 26 June 1755 at London. 16th Baroness Dacre in her own right. Married thrice;[7]
2 CONT **(1) First, to Richard Barrett-Lennard, Esq. (died 1716), son of Dacre Barrett-Lennard and his wife Jane, eldest daughter of Arthur Chichester, the second Earl of Donegal. Died a few months after his marriage to Lady Anne in 1716
2 CONC , leaving his wife with child. Their son was '''Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Baron Dacre (1717 – 12 January 1786), who died without issue'''.
2 CONT **(2) Secondly, to Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham (died 16 May 1723). Had, among other children, Charles, who m. Gertrude, sister and co-heir of John Trevor, Esq. of Glynd, in Sussex, and left at his decease, in 1754,  ....
2 CONT **(3) Thirdly, to Roger Moore, Esq., fifth son of Henry, Earl of Drogheda, in Ireland, by whom she had one son, Henry.  ....
2 CONT *References
2 CONT *1.^ June Ferguson's Royalty GED
2 CONT *2.^ From Burnet's History of his Own Times, quoted in G. Steinman's A Memoir of Barbara, Duchess of Cleveland, 1871, page 26.
2 CONT *3.^ Cunningham and Goodwin's The Story of Nell Gwyn, 1903, page 196.
2 CONT *4.^ "Memoirs of the Court of England"
2 CONT *5.^ From John Heneage Jesse's Memoirs of the Court of England During the Reign of the Stuarts, 1855, page 170.
2 CONT *6.^ [1]
2 CONT *7.^ From Booker, von Alvensleben, W Owen's The Peerage of England, Scotland, and Ireland, 1790, pages 372-374.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Lennard,_Countess_of_Sussex _____________
2 CONT *Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Thomas_Barrett-Lennard,_1st_Baronet
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron_Dacre
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/277496797/thomas-barrett-lennard
2 CONT Son of Richard Barrett and Anne Lennard, later 16th Baroness Dacre.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Educated at Harrow School.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as the 17th Baron Dacre upon the death of his mother on 26 June 1755. His mother had become suo jure Baroness Dacre in 1741 after the death of her elder sister, Lady Barbara Skelton (née Lennard), when the abeyance of
2 CONC  her father's barony was terminated in her favour. Their father's earldom, however, had become extinct upon his death in 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Anna Maria Pratt on 15 May 1739
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Barbara Barrett-Lennard (1740–1749)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT After their daughter died in 1749 ("of a sudden fever when she was only nine years old"), Thomas and Anna went on the "Grand Tour as a distraction during their recovery. After visiting Naples, Florence, Venice and other Italian ci
2 CONC ties, the couple arrived in Rome around 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT With Elizabeth FitzThomas, he had two illegitimate children, who were brought up by Lord and Lady Dacre as if they were their own:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Barrett-Lennard 1762-1857
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Barrett-Lennard 1766-1837
