2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Fitz-James_Stuart,_2nd_Duke_of_Berwick
2 CONT
2 CONT >On 31 December 1716, the 2nd Duke of Berwick became the second husband of the dowager Catalina Ventura Colón de Portugal y Ayala-Toledo, 9th Duchess of Veragua (14 July 1690 – 3 October 1739). Catalina Ventura was the daughter of
2 CONC  Pedro Manuel Colon de Portugal y de la Cueva, (25 December 1651 - 9 September 1710). This made the 2nd Duke of Berwick also duke-consort of Veragua and of la Vega.They had 6 children, of whom 4 survived to adulthood:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Fitz-James Stuart, 3rd Duke of Berwick (28 December 1718 - 30 September 1785), who on 26 July 1738 married Maria Teresa De Silva y Haro.
2 CONT # Pedro de Alcántara, (1720–1791), Captain general of the Spanish Navy, married María Benita de Rozas y Drummond, no issue.
2 CONT # Ventura (1724 - ????), married María Josefa Gagigal y Monserrat, had 1 son.
2 CONT # '''Maria Guadalupe''' (1725–1750), married to Francesco Maria Pico, Duke of Mirandola, but no issue.
