2 CONT Signature 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Élisabeth de France[1][2][3](Marie Louise Élisabeth; 14 August 1727 – 6 December 1759) was the eldest daughter of King Louis XV of France and his Queen consort, Maria Leszczyńska, and the elder twin sister of Anne Henriette
2 CONC  de France. As the daughter of the king, she was a Daughter of France (fille de France). She married Infante Philip, younger son of Philip V of Spain, and later became Duchess of Parma. In secondary sources she is referred also as
2 CONC  "Louise Élisabeth of France"[4][5]
2 CONT
