2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Louis XV
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Maria Leszczyńska
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	4 August 1729(1729-08-04)
2 CONT
2 CONT Palace of Versailles, Versailles, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	20 December 1765 (aged 36)
2 CONT
2 CONT Château de Fontainebleau, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis-Ferdinand de France,[1][2] Dauphin of France (4 September 1729 – 20 December 1765) was the only son of King Louis XV of France and his wife, Queen Maria Leszczyńska, to reach adulthood. He had a younger brother who died befo
2 CONC re his third birthday. As the son of the king, Louis was a Fils de France. He was the father of three kings of France, Louis XVI, Louis XVIII and Charles X.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
