1 NOTE GRAND DUKE OF TUSCANY
1 NOTE Ferdinand III, son of Holy Roman Emperor Leopold I, was given the Grand Duchy of Tuscanny in 1790 when his father became emperor. Ferdinand's rule lasted until 1801 when Tuscanny was taken over by the French under Napoleon, and Tu
2 CONC scanny was re-named Eturia, and part of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1814 Ferdinand III returned to the Grand Duchy of Tuscanny, replacing Napoleon's sister, Elisa Bonapart Bacciocchi as Grand Duchess, and ruled as Grand Duke until 1824, and was succeeded by his son, Leopold II.
