2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Anne Seymour-Conway was born on 1 August 1744. She was the daughter of Francis Seymour-Conway, 1st Marquess of Hertford and Lady Isabella Fitzroy.1 She married Charles Moore, 1st Marquess of Drogheda, son of Edward Moore, 5th
2 CONC  Earl of Drogheda and Lady Sarah Ponsonby, on 15 February 1766.1 She died on 4 November 1784 at age 40.1
2 CONT      As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Seymour-Conway was styled as Countess of Drogheda on 15 February 1766. From 15 February 1766, her married name became Moore. Children of Lady Anne Seymour-Conway and Charles Moore, 1st M
2 CONC arquess of Drogheda 1.Lady Frances Moore+ d. 5 Oct 1833 2.Lady Gertrude Moore2 3.Lady Anne Moore d. Feb 1788 4.unknown daughter Moore3 5.Edward Moore, 2nd Marquess of Drogheda1 b. 23 Aug 1770, d. 6 Feb 1837 6.Lady Elizabeth Emily 
2 CONC Moore+ b. 14 Mar 1771, d. 18 Mar 1841 7.Lady Mary Moore+ b. 27 Aug 1772, d. 22 Feb 1842 8.Lord Henry Seymour Moore+1 b. 1774, d. Aug 1825 9.Lady Alice Moore b. Sep 1776, d. 1789 Citations 1.[S21] L. G. Pine, The New Extinct Peerag
2 CONC e 1884-1971: Containing Extinct, Abeyant, Dormant and Suspended Peerages With Genealogies and Arms (London, U.K.: Heraldry Today, 1972), page 108. Hereinafter cited as The New Extinct Peerage. 2.[S90] Sir Bernard Burke, editor, Bu
2 CONC rke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, 53rd edition (London, U.K.: Burke's Peerage Ltd, 1891), page 446. Hereinafter cited as Burkes Peerage and Baronetage, 53rd ed. 3.[S37] Charles Mosle
2 CONC y, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1181. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,
2 CONC  107th edition.
