1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.thepeerage.com/p1206.htm#i12059]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Robert FitzGerald, 2nd Duke of Leinster was born on 12 March 1748/49 at London, England.1  He was the son of Lt.-Gen. James FitzGerald, 1st Duke of Leinster and Lady Emilia Mary Lennox.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hon. Emilia Olivia St. George, daughter of St. George Ussher St. George, 1st and last Baron St. George and Elizabeth Dominick, on 4 November 1775.3  He died on 20 October 1804 at age 55 at Carton House.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      William Robert FitzGerald, 2nd Duke of Leinster was educated at Eton College, Eton, Berkshire, England.1 He gained the rank of Cornet of Horse in 1765.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Whig) for Dublin City
2 CONC  between 1767 and 1773.1 He held the office of Sheriff of County Kildare in 1772.1 He held the office of Governor of County Kildare in 1773.1 He succeeded to the title of 7th Baron Offaly [I., 1599] on 19 November 1773.1 He succee
2 CONC ded to the title of 2nd Marquess of Kildare [I., 1761] on 19 November 1773.1 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Duke of Leinster [I., 1766] on 19 November 1773.1 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Offaly [I., 1761] on 19 Novem
2 CONC ber 1773.1 He succeeded to the title of 21st Earl of Kildare [I., 1316] on 19 November 1773.1 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount Leinster of Taplow, co. Buckingham [G.B., 1747] on 19 November 1773.1 He was invested as a Pri
2 CONC vy Counsellor (P.C.) [Ireland] in 1777.1 He was invested as a Knight, Order of St. Patrick (K.P.) in 1783.3,1 He held the office of Master of the Rolls [Ireland] between 1788 and 1789.1 He was Clerk of the Crown and Hanaper [Irela
2 CONC nd] between 1795 and 1797.1 He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.4
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Robert FitzGerald, 2nd Duke of Leinster and Hon. Emilia Olivia St. George
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Lady Emily Elizabeth FitzGerald+ 1
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Lady Isabella Charlotte FitzGerald+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Lady Mary FitzGerald+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Lord William FitzGerald+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Lady Elizabeth FitzGerald+ d. 28 Feb 18575
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.George FitzGerald, Marquess of Kildare b. 20 Jun 1783, d. Feb 17841
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.Lady Cecilia Olivia Geraldine FitzGerald+ b. 3 Mar 1786, d. 27 Jul 18631
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.Lady Olivia Letitia Catherine FitzGerald+ b. 9 Sep 1787, d. 28 Feb 18581
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.Augustus Frederick FitzGerald, 3rd Duke of Leinster+ b. 21 Aug 1791, d. 10 Oct 18741
2 CONT
2 CONT **************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_FitzGerald,_2nd_Duke_of_Leinster]
2 CONT
2 CONT FitzGerald made his Grand Tour between 1768 and 1769. During the same time, he also was Member of Parliament (MP) for Kildare Borough. FitzGerald sat in the Irish House of Commons for Dublin City from 1676 until 1773, when he took
2 CONC  on his father's title and estates. Politically he was a liberal supporter of Henry Grattan and co-founded the Irish Whig Club in 1789. He controlled usually six Kildare members of the Irish House of Commons. In 1770 FitzGerald wa
2 CONC s chosen Grandmaster of the Grand Lodge of Ireland, which post he held for two years.[1] He was reelected for another year in 1777.[1] FitzGerald was a supporter of the Catholic Emancipation and helped to found the Catholic semina
2 CONC ry at Maynooth in 1795. Withdrawing from parliament with Grattan in 1797, he moved to England to be with his sick wife and remained there during the 1798 rebellion.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second, but eldest surviving, son of James FitzGerald, 1st Duke of Leinster and the well-connected Lady Emily Mary Lennox. On 4 November 1775 he married Hon. Emilia Olivia St. George, daughter of St George Saint-George,
2 CONC  1st Baron St George and Elizabeth Dominick.[2] He was also the elder brother of the 1790s revolutionary Lord Edward FitzGerald, and was a first cousin of the English liberal politician Charles James Fox.
2 CONT
2 CONT His homes were at Carton in County Kildare and Leinster House in Dublin. He was a founder member of the Order of St Patrick in 1783 and of the Royal Irish Academy (1785), and was a large investor in the Royal Canal company launche
2 CONC d in 1790. His family's estates of 60,000 acres (25,000 Ha) in Kildare were in three parts, around Maynooth, Rathangan and Athy. He rebuilt the main bridge in Athy over the River Barrow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: http://www.cracoftspeerage.co.uk]
2 CONT
2 CONT born13 Mar 1748/9
2 CONT
2 CONT mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Nov 1775 Hon Emilia Olivia Usher-St George (d. 23 Jun 1798), only dau. and hrss. of St George [Usher-St George], 1st Baron St George, by his wife Elizabeth Dominick, dau. and hrss. of Christopher Dominick, of Dublin
2 CONT
2 CONT children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lord George FitzGerald, styled Marquess of Kildare (b. 20 Jun 1783; dvp. Feb 1784)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Lord Augustus Frederick FitzGerald, later 3rd Duke of Leinster
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Lord William Butler, mar., and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lady Mary Rebecca FitzGerald (b. 6 May 1777; d. 28 Feb 1842), mar. 15 Apr 1799 as his second wife Sir Charles Lockhart-Ross, 7th Bt., of Balnagowan and Bonnington, co. Ross, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Lady Emily Elizabeth FitzGerald, mar. 1801 John Joseph Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Lady Cecilia Olivia Geraldine FitzGerald (b. 3 Mar 1786;  d. 27 Jul 1863), mar. 18 Aug 1806 Thomas [Foley], 3rd Baron Foley, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Lady Olivia Letitia Catherine FitzGerald (b. 9 Sep 1787;  d. 29 Feb 1858), mar. 8 May 1806 Charles [Kinnaird], 8th Lord Kinnaird, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Lady Isabelle FitzGerald, mar. 1 Jun 1809 Louis Guy Charles Gullaume de Rohan-Chabot, Comte de Jarnac (b. 1780;  d. 1875)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Lady Elizabeth Mary FitzGerald (d. 28 Feb 1857), mar. 22 Jul 1805 Lt Col Sir Edward Littlehales later Baker, 1st Bt., of Ranston, co. Dorset (d. 4 Mar 1825), and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT died 20 Oct 1804
2 CONT
2 CONT note
2 CONT
2 CONT Member of Parliament for the City of Dublin 1767-73;  Grand Master of Freemasons [I] 1770-72 and 1777-78;  Sheriff of co. Kildare 1772;  a Governor of co. Kildare 1773;  Privy Councillor [I] 1777;  Founder Knight of St Patrick 178
2 CONC 3;  Master of the Rolls [I] 1788-89 and Clerk of the Crown and Hanaper [I] 1795-97
