1 NOTE The Grand Duchy of Tuscanny passed from Ferdinand III to his son, Leopold II in 1824. Grand Duke Leopold II ruled until 1848, and due to the revolutionary movement of the times, was forced to flee in 1849 to Gaeta, and he returned
2 CONC  a few months later under protection of Austria. He had granted a constitution in 1848, but withdrew it in 1852, and in 1859 was obliged by the pro-Italian fervor to leave again. Although the French put on pressure to restore Leop
2 CONC old, the people of Tuscanny voted to join with the Kingdom of Sardinia, and became part of the Kingdom of Italy under Emmanuel.
