2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  Henry Scott, 3rd Duke of Buccleuch was born on 2 September 1746.2 He was the son of Francis Scott, Earl of Dalkeith and Caroline Campbell, Baroness Greenwich.2,1 He was baptised on 29 September 1746 at St. George's Church, St. Ge
2 CONC orge Street, Hanover Square, London, England.2 He married Lady Elizabeth Montagu, daughter of George Montagu, 1st Duke of Montagu and Lady Mary Montagu, on 2 May 1767 at Montagu House, London, England.2 He died on 11 January 1812 
2 CONC at age 65 at Dalkeith Castle, Scotland.2 He was buried at Dalkeith Castle, Scotland.2 His will was probated in June 1812.2      Henry Scott, 3rd Duke of Buccleuch succeeded to the title of 6th Earl of Buccleuch [S., 1619] on 22 Ap
2 CONC ril 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Baron Scott of Tindall, Northumberland [E., 1663] on 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 7th Lord Scott of Buccleuch [S., 1606] on 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 6
2 CONC th Baron Scott of Quhitchester and Eskdaill [S., 1619] on 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Doncaster, co. York [E., 1663] on 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Duke of Buccleuch [S., 1663] on 
2 CONC 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Dalkeith [S., 1663] on 22 April 1751.2 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Scott of Whitchester and Eskdale [S., 1663] on 22 April 1751.2 He was educated at Eton College, 
2 CONC Eton, Berkshire, England.2 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Thistle (K.T.) on 23 December 1767.2 He held the office of Governor of the Royal Bank of Scotland between 1777 and 1812.2 In 1778 he raised a regiment of Fencibl
2 CONC es.2 He held the office of Captain General of the Royal Company of Archers between 1778 and 1812.2 He held the office of President of the Royal Society of Edinburgh between 1783 and 1812.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of 
2 CONC Haddington between 1794 and 1812.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Midlothian between 1794 and 1812.2 On 11 January 1794 he inherited his mother's estates.2 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) on 28 Ma
2 CONC y 1794 when he resigned the Order of the Thistle.2 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Roxburghshire between 1804 and 1812.2 He succeeded to the title of 5th Duke of Queensberry on 23 December 1810. Children of Henry Scott, 3
2 CONC rd Duke of Buccleuch and Lady Elizabeth Montagu 	1	Lady Elizabeth Scott+3 d. 29 Jun 1837 	2	George Scott, Earl of Dalkeith4 b. 25 Mar 1768, d. 29 May 1768 	3	Lady Mary Scott+3 b. 21 May 1769, d. 21 Apr 1823 	4	Charles William Henr
2 CONC y Montagu-Scott, 4th Duke of Buccleuch+4 b. 24 May 1772, d. 20 Apr 1819 	5	Lady Caroline Scott+3 b. 6 Jul 1774, d. 29 Apr 1854 	6	Henry James Montagu-Scott, 2nd Baron Montagu of Boughton+3 b. 16 Dec 1776, d. 30 Oct 1845 	7	Lady Ha
2 CONC rriet Scott+3 b. 1 Dec 1780, d. 18 Apr 1833
2 CONT
