1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/128482272 The first physician in Terre Haute, IN arriving in the either 1816 or 1817 after acquiring his medical training in Cincinnati. One account says that he owned one of but
2 CONC  two cabins in Terre Haute in 1817. He also established the first ferry across the Wabash River in Terre Haute at the foot of what today is Ohio Street. Built a log home at the corner of Second and Ohio Streets.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although he continued to practice medicine, he was perhaps more prominent as an astute businessman acquiring much property in a growing Terre Haute and surrounding areas in Vigo and Clay counties. Overall, a very well respected le
2 CONC ader of early Terre Haute.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Rebecca Modesitt 1788–1830
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Ann Modesitt Warren 1813–1903 Frances Ann Modesitt Warren
2 CONT Birth: 24 Sep 1813 Hardy County, West Virginia, USA
