1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vice-Admiral Sir George Tyler''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: 28 December 1792 at Cottrell, Glamorgan, Wales.
2 CONT * Parents: Admiral Sir Charles Tyler and Margaret Leach. 
2 CONT * Baptised: 24 January 1797 at St. Mary, Pembrokeshire, Wales.
2 CONT * Wife: Harriet Margaret Sullivan, daughter of Rt. Hon. John Sullivan and Lady Henrietta Hobart, on 21 September 1819.
2 CONT * Death: 4 June 1862 at age 69 at Dunravin Castle, Glamorgan, Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was educated on 3 October 1806 at Royal Naval College, Portsmouth, Hampshire, England.
2 CONT * He was commissioned on 7 December 1809, in the service of the Royal Navy.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Midshipman before May 1811 in the service of the on board H.M.S. Spartan.
2 CONT * In May 1811 he lost his right arm, in a boat affair in Quiberon Bay.
2 CONT *  He gained the rank of Lieutenant on 6 February 1813.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Commander on 7 February 1815.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Post-Captain on 10 October 1822.
2 CONT * He held the office of Justice of the Peace (J.P.).
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Rear-Admiral on 26 October 1852.
2 CONT * He gained the rank of Vice-Admiral on 8 December 1857.
2 CONT * He held the office of Deputy Lieutenant (D.L.).
2 CONT * He was invested as a Knight, Hanoverian Order (K.H.).
2 CONT * He lived at Cottrell, Glamorgan, Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Vice-Admiral Sir George Tyler and Harriet Margaret Sullivan
2 CONT * Louisa Tyler d. 4 Oct 1915
2 CONT * Augustus Tyler
2 CONT * Harriet Georgina Tyler
2 CONT * Anne Maria Tyler d. 1 Sep 1886
2 CONT * George Henry Tyler b. 28 Feb 1824
2 CONT * Charles Frederick Tyler b. 20 Sep 1825
2 CONT * Gwinnett Tyler b. 25 Feb 1828, d. Mar 1886
2 CONT * Reverend Edward Octavious Tyler b. 25 Sep 1830, d. 28 Jul 1895
2 CONT * Alfred Tyler b. 19 Nov 1830
2 CONT * John Hobart Tyler b. 18 Oct 1831, d. Mar 1918
2 CONT * St. Vincent Tyler b. 12 Dec 1834, d. 25 Aug 1869
2 CONT * Caroline Tyler b. 1835, d. 22 Oct 1898
2 CONT
2 CONT REF: [http://www.thepeerage.com/p7465.htm#i74649 The Peerage]
