1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Thomas Brand, 20th Lord Dacre1
2 CONT *''''''M, #73456, b. 25 March 1774, d. 21 March 1851
2 CONT *Last Edited=21 Feb 2011
2 CONT *''''''     Thomas Brand, 20th Lord Dacre was born on 25 March 1774 at The Hoo, Hertfordshire, England.1 He was the son of Thomas Brand and Gertrude Roper, Baroness Dacre.1 He married Barberina Ogle, daughter of Admiral Sir Chalon
2 CONC er Ogle, 1st Bt. and Hester Thomas, on 4 December 1819.1 He died on 21 March 1851 at age 76 at The Hoo, Hertfordshire, England.1
2 CONT *''''''     He was a practising barrister in 1800.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Whig) for Hertfordshire between 1807 and 1819.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Whig) for Helston between Ja
2 CONC nuary 1807 and April 1807.1 He succeeded to the title of 20th Lord Dacre [E., 1321] on 3 October 1819.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1014. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p7346.htm#i73456
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT ====Thomas Brand, 20th Baron Dacre (25 March 1774 – 21 March 1851) was a British peer and Whig politician.
2 CONT ====Dacre was the eldest son of Thomas Brand, of The Hoo, Hertfordshire, and Gertrude, 19th Baroness Dacre, daughter of the Hon. Charles Roper.
2 CONT ====Dacre entered Parliament for Helston in January 1807, a seat he only held until May of the same year, when he was returned for Hertfordshire. He continued to represent this constituency until 1819, when he succeeded his mother
2 CONC  in the barony of Dacre and entered the House of Lords.
2 CONT ====Lord Dacre married Barbarina, daughter of Admiral Sir Chaloner Ogle, 1st Baronet and widow of Valentine Wilmot, in 1819. The marriage was childless. He died at The Hoo, Hertfordshire, in March 1851, aged 76, and was succeeded 
2 CONC in the barony by his younger brother, Henry. Lady Dacre died in London in May 1854, aged 86.
2 CONT ====References
2 CONT *Leigh Rayment's Peerage Pages [self-published source?][better source needed]
2 CONT *Leigh Rayment's Historical List of MPs
2 CONT ====External links
2 CONT *Hansard 1803–2005: contributions in Parliament by Thomas Brand
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Brand,_20th_Baron_Dacre
2 CONT *______________
