1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry William Stanhope was born in London on August 2, 1790. He was baptised in Westminster Abbey on September 21, 1790. His parents were General Charles Stanhope the 3rd Earl of Harrington and Jane Fleming the dau
2 CONC ghter of First Baronet Fleming. He graduated with a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) in 1812 and a Master of Arts (M.A.) in 1814 at Trinity Hall, Cambridge University.
2 CONT He was the non-resident Rector at Gawsworth, Cheshire from 1827 to 1872 (45 years). He was also the Rector at Chesham in Buckinghamshire from 1826 to 1847 (21 years). His address in 1861 was 23 Spring Gardens in St Martins-in-the-
2 CONC Fields, London (in 2026 the Russian Embassy). By 1871 and near death he moved next door to 25 Spring Gardens in St Martin's-in-the-Fields, London.
2 CONT Reverend Stanhope married his first wife Grace Aguilar Stanhope in Westminster Abbey circa 1852. She is understood to have passed away circa 1858 some 4-5 years after the birth of their only child, a daughter named Adeline Stanhop
2 CONC e, who was later raised by family friend Fanny Copere from the age of six to nine by which time Reverend Stanhope decided to re-marry second wife Paris cabaret fashion designer Fanny Copere in 1862 to give Adeline some semblance o
2 CONC f stability and a loving pair of parents with the blessing of the late Grace (no relation to the Jewish historian of the same name, Grace Aguilar). Reverend Stanhope predeceased his second wife, dying aged 81 in London on June 21,
2 CONC  1872. 
