1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Colonel Sir Horace Beauchamp Seymour KCH (22 November 1791 – 23 November 1851) was a Peelite Member of Parliament for Lisburn 1819–26, Orfor (1820), Bodmin (1826–32), Midhurst (1841–45), Antrim (1845–47), and Lisburn 1847–51. He w
2 CONC as an ancestor of Diana, Princess of Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Horace Seymour was the son of Admiral Lord Hugh Seymour (son of Francis Seymour-Conway, 1st Marquess of Hertford) and Lady Anne Horatia Waldegrave. He married, firstly, Elizabeth Malet Palk, daughter of Sir Lawrence Palk, 2nd Baro
2 CONC net and granddaughter of Robert Palk, on 15 May 1818. He married, secondly, Frances Selina Isabella Poyntz, daughter of William Stephen Poyntz and Hon. Elizabeth Mary Browne, in July 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Colonel Sir Horace Beauchamp Seymour''' was born on November 22, 1791, in Frome, Somerset, England. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-20201237 Vice-Adm. Lord Hugh Seymour] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-20201238
2 CONC  Lady Anne Horatia Seymour (Waldegrave)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Horace married [https://www.geni.com/profile-66173380 Frances Selina Isabella Seymour] on July 9, 1835, in St James, Westminster, Middlesex, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Horace married [https://www.geni.com/profile-20200496 Elizabeth Malet Seymour, Countess of Rochester] on May 15, 1818, in England. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-37038740 Lt.-Col. Charles Francis Seymour]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-37038741 Admiral Frederick Beauchamp Paget Seymour, 1st Baron Alcester, GCB]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-41355299 Adelaide Spencer, Dowager Countess Spencer]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-66174683 Gertrude Elizabeth Seymour]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10105.htm#i101046
2 CONT ====================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
2 CONT He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.)He was appointed Knight Commander, Hanoverian Order (K.C.H.)6 He gained the rank of Colonel in the British Army.
2 CONT
