1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Calvert-2403
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Calvert) Steuart was a Maryland colonist.Elizabeth Calvert was born in around 1750 - 1760. She was the daughter of Benedict Swingate Calvert, a Loyalist politician and planter and the illegitimate son of Charles Calvert
2 CONC , 5th Baron Baltimore, and Elizabeth Calvert (1731 – 1788), who was the daughter of Maryland Governor Captain Charles Calvert and Rebecca Gerard, and a wealthy heiress in colonial Maryland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1761 her portrait was painted by the noted painter John Hesselius, along with her sister Eleanor and brother Charles. The portrait hangs in the Baltimore Museum of Art.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Calvert married the physician Charles Mark Steuart (abt. 1750 - abt. 1798), the son of the politician and Edinburgh physician George Hume Steuart and his wife Anne Digges. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Calvert and Charles Mark Steuart had a number of children, including the physician 
2 CONT # Charles Calvert Steuart, (abt. 1784 - 1836).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Calvert Steuart died in 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
