2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor married Dr. David Stuart, an Alexandria physician, in the Autumn 1783. David became the executor of the Custis estate and legal guardian to the children. Her two elder daughters, Elizabeth and Martha, lived with Eleanor an
2 CONC d David at Abingdon, while her younger two children, Eleanor and Wash, lived with their grandparents George and Martha Washington at Mount Vernon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor and David had five daughters and two sons of their own:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Calvert Stuart Robinson (born 1784), married William Robinson Sarah Stuart Waite (born 1786), married Obed Waite Ariana Calvert Stuart William Skolto Stuart[3][9] Eleanor Custis Stuart (born 1792) Charles Calvert Stuart (1794–
2 CONC 1846), married Cornelia Lee Rosalie Eugenia Stuart Webster (1796–1886), married William Greenleaf Webster
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor and David resided at two estates in Fairfax County, Virginia: Hope Park and Ossian Hall. She died at age 53 at Tudor Place, the home of her daughter Martha Parke Custis Peter, on 28 September 1811.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	1754 Death: 	Sep. 28, 1811
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried under the chancel rail in vault with parents Benedict L. Calvert and wife Elizabeth. (1754 - Sept. 28, 1811) Eleanor was first married to Col. John Parke Custis, step son of General Washington. After his death in 1781 she m
2 CONC arried her cousin Dr. David Stuart. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Married John Parke Custis, son of Martha Custis Washington and stepson of George Washington, in 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
