1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Herbert,_12th_Earl_of_Pembroke
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Henry Herbert, 12th Earl of Pembroke and 9th Earl of Montgomery (19 September 1791 – 25 April 1862) was a British nobleman in line for great estates and position as head of the distinguished Herbert family and heir to the e
2 CONC arldom of Pembroke, but lived an irregular life in exile after a dissolute youth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 12th Earl of Pembroke, 10th Creation 9th Earl of Montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of George Augustus Herbert, 11th Earl of Pembroke and 8th Earl of Montgomery, and his first wife Elizabeth Beauclerk. Paternal grandson of Henry Herbert, 10th Earl of Pembroke and 7th Earl of Montgomery, and his first wife The
2 CONC  Lady Elizabeth Spencer. Maternal grandson of Topham Beauclerk and The Lady Diana Spencer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both of Robert's grandmothers were sisters - the daughters of Charles Spencer, 3rd Duke of Marlborough, and his wife the Honourable Elizabeth Trevor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to his father's titles in 1827, and was living in Paris by 1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ottavia Spinelli (1779–1857) in 1814, a Sicilian princess and the daughter of the Duke of Laurino. The marriage was annulled in 1818 at the insistence of Robert's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert never remarried and lived the remainder of his life in Paris. He had seven illegitimate children by two mistresses, and upon his death he was succeeded by his half-nephew George, 13th Earl of Pembroke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Alexina Sophia Gallot:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Henry Gallot Granville Montgomery Sidney George Granville Montgomery Ida Alexina Gallot Granville
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Marie Catherine Caroline Schäffer:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henriette de Montgomery Henri Georges de Pembroke de Montgomery Henri Adolphus de Montgomery Henriette Marie Jeanne de Montgomery
