1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Conolly
2 CONT
2 CONT John Conolly (27 May 1794 – 5 March 1866) was an English psychiatrist. He published the volume Indications of Insanity in 1830. In 1839, he was appointed resident physician to the Middlesex County Asylum where he introduced the pr
2 CONC inciple of non-restraint into the treatment of the insane, which led to non-restraint became accepted practice throughout England. With colleagues he founded the 'Provincial Medical and Surgical Association', and founded the 'Brit
2 CONC ish and Foreign Medical Review, or, A Quarterly Journal of Practical Medicine'.
