1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lord Sussex Lennox (11 June 1802 – 12 April 1874), also known as Lord Sussex Lennox of Richmond,[1] was an English cricketer. He was associated with Marylebone Cricket Club and was recorded in one first-class match
2 CONC  in 1826, totalling 5 runs with a highest score of 3 and holding no catches.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married the Hon. Mary Lawless, daughter of Valentine Lawless, 2nd Baron Cloncurry, and his first wife Elizabeth Georgiana Morgan, and had three children, Sussex junior, Berkeley and Charles. The marriage caused some comment as 
2 CONC Mary had divorced her first husband, Henry Fock, 3rd Baron De Robeck, to marry him, an unusual step for the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Sussex_Lennox
