1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of PRIVATE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A094661  DAR Ancestor # A094661]
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/19207061/reuben-ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Reuben & Frances Ratliff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married his cousin, Phoebe Ratliff on July 1, 1786 in Franklin Co., VA d/o Silas Ratliff & Elizabeth?
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. War soldier
2 CONT
2 CONT Sept 1776 - in services of Capt. Gilbert Christy of Long Island on the Holston River, Washington Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT May 1781 - Spy and Ranger under Capt. Arter & Col. Green against the Tories, Henry County, NC. Fought until 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his discharge, he moved to Russell, Tazwell Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moved to Morgan Co. ca 1835. Found in the 1850 Census for Morgan Co., VA, living with his daughter Hannah & her husband, David Lykins.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is much confusion over his birth year. According to the DAR headstone, it was 1759. According to the math (d.1852 at age 84) it would have been 1768. According to the Census records, it is 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT If he was 84 at the time of his death, as his original headstone states, then he would have been born in 1768 or possibly 1767, depending on the month.
