1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A History of Kentucky Baptists From 1769 to 1885, Including More Than 800 Biographical Sketches, J. H. Spencer, Manuscript Revised and Corrected by Mrs. Burilla B. Spencer, In Two Volumes. Printed For the Author. 1
2 CONC 886. Republished By Church History Research & Archives 1976 Lafayette, Tennessee. Vol. 2, p 113 [Barren County].
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM RATLIFF was one of the early preachers in Green River Association. He was ordained to the ministry at Blue Spring church, in Barren county, in 1806. He was immediately called to the pastoral care of this church, and served
2 CONC  it some ten or a dozen years, when he was called to his reward. He had the reputation of being a good, faithful man. It is regretted that so little is now known of him. Some of his posterity still live around old Blue Spring  ...
2 CONC ... BLUE SPRING (1799)
2 CONT
2 CONT Blue Spring Church was organized in 1799 in what is now Metcalfe County (but at the time it was in Barren County). The first pastor was Elder Elijah Summers, who served in that capacity until 1806. Elder William Ratliff then serve
2 CONC d, until 1814. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Rev. William Ratliff Sr. was born on 6 October 1762, in Virginia, British Colonial America, his father, Reuben Henry Ratliff Sr., was 30 and his mother, Frances Holloway, was 28. He married Mary Margaret Hinson in 1794, in Gr
2 CONC een, Kentucky, United States. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 1 daughter. He lived in Anson, North Carolina, United States in 1800. He died on 2 July 1816, in Barren, Kentucky, United States, at the age of 53, and was
2 CONC  buried in Barren, Kentucky, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was an ordained minister of the regular Baptist and performed several marriages in Barren County before his death in 1816. His widow Margaret, married Levi Blunt and they moved to Mason/Menard counties Illinois about 1834.
2 CONC  Most of William and Margaret's children moved to Missouri - James, Jordon, Jonathan, Mary, wife of Richard Bradley, and William. Stephen stayed in Barren & Metcalf County KY and Alexander moved to Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT METCALFE COUNTY KENTUCKY CEMETERY RECORDS IV copyright 1983 Metcalfe County Historical Society McDowell Publications Route 4 Box 314 Utica, KY 42376 Page 16:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cemetery, Center, KY Ratliff grave: date copied November 4, 1977 located: on Main Street in Center on left hand side as you travel N.E. on Hwy 314. Number of graves identifiable by inscription = 1. Number of graves unidentifiable 
2 CONC by inscription = 2. Cemetery no longer receiving burials William Ratliff born: Oct 6, 1762 died: July 2, 1816  [near post office building]
2 CONT
2 CONT Full Name: William Ratliff Date Born: 06 Oct 1762 Place Born: Virginia Date Died: 02 Jul 1816 Place Buried: Center, Barren Co. , Ky. Sex: Male Occupation: Minister Religion: Baptist No. of Marriages: One Who Married: Mary/Margaret
2 CONC  Hinson When Married: About 1790 Where Married: Anson County, NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Number of Children:
2 CONT
