2 CONT moved to Mason/Menard counties Illinois about 1834. Most of William and
2 CONT Margaret's children moved to Missouri - James, Jordon, Jonathan, Mary, wife of
2 CONT Richard Bradley, and William. Stephen stayed in Barren & Metcalf County
2 CONT KY and Alexander moved to Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT METCALFE COUNTY KENTUCKY CEMETERY RECORDS IV copyright 1983 Metcalfe County Historical Society McDowell Publications Route 4 Box 314 Utica, KY 42376 Page 16:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cemetery, Center, KY Ratliff grave: date copied November 4, 1977 located: on Main Street in Center on left hand side as you travel N.E. on Hwy 314. Number of graves identifiable by inscription = 1. Number of graves unidentifiable 
2 CONC by inscription = 2. Cemetery no longer receiving burials William Ratliff born: Oct 6, 1762 died: July 2, 1816 
2 CONT [near post office building]
2 CONT
2 CONT , 
2 CONT
2 CONT William was an 
2 CONT Full Name: William Ratliff
2 CONT Date Born: 06 Oct 1762
2 CONT Place Born: Virginia
2 CONT Date Died: 02 Jul 1816
2 CONT Place Buried: Center, Barren Co. , Ky. 
2 CONT Sex: Male
2 CONT Occupation: Minister
2 CONT Religon: Baptist
2 CONT No. of Marriages: One
2 CONT Who Married: Mary/Margaret Hinson
2 CONT When Married: About 1790
2 CONT Where Married: Anson County, NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Number of Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT James Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT William Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT Jordan Ratliff*
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Ratliff
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret HINSON and William RATLIFF are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Stephen A. RATLIFF was born 28 Jun 1795 in Green Co. KY, and died 13 Jul 1859 in Barren Co. KY. He married Martha "Patsy "A. BRADLEY 26 Aug 1819 in Barren Co. KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. James RATLIFF was born 19 Jan 1798 in Barren Co. KY, and died 16 Apr 1860 in Macon Co. MO. He married Martha "Patsy" HIND 18 Mar 1817 in Barren County KY, daughter of Samuel HIND and Margaret "Peggy" Willis Arnold. She was bor
2 CONC n 29 Jun 1799 in Near Horse Cave KY, and died 5 Jun 1880 in New Boston MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Mary RATLIFF was born 26 Dec 1800 in Barren Co. KY, and died 23 Feb 1864 in Randolph Co. MO. She married Richard BRADLEY 25 Feb 1818 in Barren Co. KY. He was born 27 Dec 1795 in Barren Co. KY, and died 25 Jul 1865 in Randolph
2 CONC  Co. MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. William RATLIFF was born in Barren Co. KY, and died 1860 . He married Mary "Polly" PHILPOT 27 Nov 1826 in Barren Co. Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Jonathan RATLIFF was born in BARREN CO. KY, and died 13 Nov 1881 in BENTON CO. ARK. He married Dulaney Crawford ROWLAND 15 Dec 1829 in Randolph Co. MO. She was born 16 Dec 1807 in TN, and died 5 Jul 1899 in Garfield, AR.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. *Jordan RATLIFF was born  in Barren Co. Kentucky, and died 1840 in Randolph County Missouri. He married Lavinia ROWLAND 20 Sep 1831 in Randolph County MO. She was born 1815 in TN, and died in Macon Co. MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. Alexander RATLIFF was born  in Barren Co. KY, and died ABT 1879 in Atkinson County Missouri.He married ? Rachel Atwell. He married second to Leanna Bunch Jun 1864 in Burlington Kansas. She was born 31 Dec 1830 in Tennessee, a
2 CONC nd died 19 Aug 1906 in Atchinson County Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT A History of Kentucky Baptists From 1769 to 1885, Including More Than 800 Biographical Sketches, J. H. Spencer, Manuscript Revised and Corrected by Mrs. Burilla B. Spencer, In Two Volumes. Printed For the Author. 1886. Republished
2 CONC  By Church History Research & Archives 1976 Lafayette, Tennessee. Vol. 2, p 113 [Barren County]
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM RATLIFF was one of the early preachers in Green River Association. He was ordained to the ministry at Blue Spring church, in Barren county, in 1806. He was immediately called to the pastoral care of this church, and served
2 CONC  it some ten or a dozen years, when he was called to his reward. He had the reputation of being a good, faithful man. It is regretted that so little is now know of him. Some of his posterity still live around old Blue Spring Churc
2 CONC h.
2 CONT
2 CONT ///
2 CONT
2 CONT 1828 court document reference, from August County VA, for Margaret, now Blount, formerly married to William Ratliff, and Stephen Ratliff, both handling William's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of William Ratliff in 2 Jul 1816 in Barren Co. KY , his widow , Margaret married Levi Blount
2 CONT 6 Feb 1828 in Barren Co. Kentucky. Right about 1830, they moved to Menard/Mason Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT She wished to be relieved of the responsibility of infants[infants: age 0-14] William, Jonathan, Jordon, and Alexander in a deed dated February 1828 (book L Page 226). This was an agreement between her and her oldest son, Stephen,
2 CONC  and it states that she is the widow of William Ratliff deceased
