1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Waldegrave,_8th_Earl_Waldegrave
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice-Admiral William Waldegrave, 8th Earl Waldegrave, CB (27 October 1788 – 24 October 1859) was a British naval commander and politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Waldegrave was the son of the 4th Earl Waldegrave and was educated at Eton. In 1802, he became a Midshipman in the Royal Navy, rising to the ranks of Lieutenant in 1806 and Commander in 1809. He fought during the War of 1812, comm
2 CONC anding frigate HMS Macedonian (which was later captured by the United States).
2 CONT
2 CONT On his return to England, he married Elizabeth Whitbread, the daughter of Samuel Whitbread and took over from his father-in-law's post as Member of Parliament (MP) for Bedford in 1815.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leaving that post in 1818, Waldegrave then commanded HMS Seringapatam from 1829–32 and HMS Revenge from 1839–42 and was created a Companion of the Order of the Bath in 1840.
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired from the navy in 1842 as a Rear-Admiral, inherited his childless nephew's titles in 1846 and was married for a second time that year, to Sarah Milward, née Whitear. He was promoted to Vice-Admiral in 1858 and died a yea
2 CONC r later, three days before his seventy-first birthday. His eldest son, William Waldegrave, Viscount Chewton had died in 1854 and he was succeeded by his grandson, William.
