1 CONT Birth: 1710 in England Note:
1 CONT BIOGRAPHY: After Rob was convicted of murder and sent to America, Jenny wanted to follow him to Virginia. She knew a girlfriend, Evelyn Byrd, in Virginia and on March 1, 1726, Jenny left England to go visit Evelyn and look for Rob
1 CONC . Jenny arrived in Virginia April 20, 1726 with the William Byrd family aboard the ship "Randolph" and sailed up the James River in Virginia. Jenny found Rob but he had years still to serve, so Jenny had to buy his freedom. She pa
1 CONC id 50 golden English guineas for him and he was freed on Monday, May 1, 1726 and they were married. They moved to Albemarle County, Virginia, settled on Slate River where Rob built their first home and called the homeplace Snowden
1 CONC . The town still goes by the name Snowden. Rob and Jenny had four (4) sons. Two (2) of their sons, William and James, took their mother's surname, spelling it Ratclyffe. Because of the Radclyffe history they wanted to pass the nam
1 CONC e on to future generations.-------------------------------------------------------------------Susan Ratliff McClung; "Some Descendants of Alexander Rufus Ratliff" by Larry Franklin Ratliff; "Our Ratliff Roots and Some Descendants 
1 CONC of Jacob M. Ratliff" by Larry Franklin Ratliff; Kathleen Ratliff Reynolds; Evelyn Ratliff Hurst; Maxine Ratliff Kershner; Mae Hartz Ratliff; Anna Acord Ratliff; "My Ratliff Family, 1730's-1990" by Ralph Hellier Ratliff, 1991; "New
1 CONC  Dictionary of American Family Names" by Elsdon C. Smith, 1973; "Richard Ratcliff of Lancashire, England and Talbot County, Maryland and his Ancestors and Descendants, 1066-1966" by Clarence Earl Ratcliff; Union, West Virginia Cou
1 CONC rt House; "Loudoun County Marriages, 1760-1850" by John Vogt and T. William Kethley Jr., 1984; "Pulaski County Marriages, 1839-1857" by John Vogt and T. William Kethley Jr., 1984; "Devil Water" by Anya Seton; Ralph Hellier Ratliff
1 CONC ; "Keepers of the Name and the Blood: History of Redclyffe, Radcliff, Ratcliffe, and Ratliff Family," 1992; Frances Arrigo Ratliff
