0 @N6000000007329564833@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT From the House of Bourbon;  Reign: 1793-95 (Technically, he never reigned);
1 CONT According to official reports, he died of tuberculosis while a prisoner of the
1 CONT Republican governemtn in Paris.  Many believed that he had escaped. Later,
1 CONT more that 30 people claimed to be the "Lost Dauphin."
0 @N6000000002322320188@ NOTE As elector Frederick Augustus III from 1763, he brought order and efficiency
1 CONT to his country's finances and administration. He declined the Polish crown in
1 CONT 1791. When he made peace with Napoleon, Napoleon secured the grand duchy of
1 CONT warsaw (1807) for him as well as the title of King of Saxony (1806). Frederick
1 CONT remained a loyal ally to him after the disastrous Russian campaign (1812-13).
1 CONT In the Battle of Leipzig (Oct 1813) he was taken prisoner and later he lost
1 CONT three-fifths of his territory to Prussia. See Frederick Augustus II #1897.
