0 @N6000000002188370254@ NOTE Emperor of Austria from 1835 to 1848, son and successor of Emperor Francis I (who also, as Francis II, had been the last Holy Roman emperor). A well-meaning monarch in his lucid moments, he was subject to fits of insanity. A counc
1 CONC il of state that included Metternich governed in his name. After revolution broke out in Vienna in 1848 the emperor promulgated (April) a constitution, but it failed to satisfy the revolutionists. He fled from Vienna in May and—af
1 CONC ter the recapture of Vienna by Windischgrätz—was persuaded by Felix of Schwarzenberg to abdicate (Dec. 2, 1848) in favor of his nephew, Francis Joseph.
