0 @N6000000003216061608@ NOTE Daughter of 1st Earl of Lucan.  The original seat of the Bingham family was a castle which had been "burnt many years" when Robert Daniel Beaufort came to Castlebar House, Castlebar, Co Mayo in 1787.  All that remained of it then 
1 CONC was "two great round towers", one of which had rooms added to it either side by a long corridor by the Lord Lucan of the time, who was 1st Earl; Dr Beaufort described them as "tolerably good and convenient, furnished with some pic
1 CONC tures of which a few have merit"; although he regarded the furnishing as "far from elegant".  This adequate, if somewhat makeshift dewlling was destroyed in the rebellion of 1798 and replaced by a house that had even less pretensi
1 CONC ons of being a nobleman's house.
