0 @N6000000002322303162@ NOTE Founder of the Brazilian empire and first emperor of Brazil, from Dec 01 1822
1 CONT to Apr 07 1831, also reckoned as King of Portugal. When Napoleon conquered
1 CONT Portugal in 1807, Peter accompanied the royal family in its flight to Brazil.
1 CONT He remained there as regent when King John returned to Portugal in 1821. He
1 CONT antagonized his Brazilian subjects by his continuing interests in Portuguese
1 CONT affairs and was forced to abdicate in 1831 in favor of his son, Dom Pedro II
1 CONT (Peter) five years old. Peter I then returned to Portugal.
0 @N6000000002176654394@ NOTE Founder of the Brazilian empire and first emperor of Brazil, from Dec 01 1822
1 CONT to Apr 07 1831, also reckoned as King of Portugal. When Napoleon conquered
1 CONT Portugal in 1807, Peter accompanied the royal family in its flight to Brazil.
1 CONT He remained there as regent when King John returned to Portugal in 1821. He
